{
  "layoutId": "Layout-204",
  "name": "Garden House — Multi-Zone Flanking",
  "description": "A single-storey 13-room family home, zoned like an architect would: a south-facing day/service band (Living → Dining → Kitchen → Pantry/Powder — the noisy + wet zone) and a cool, quiet north band of bedrooms, study, ensuite and family bath, joined by a central hallway spine. Bedrooms are buffered north, but a deliberate Kitchen→Hallway door lets kitchen noise and odour flank through the spine toward the private rooms, and the windowless interior Study sits right off the hallway — rich transmissive conflicts (acoustic / olfactory / thermal) across many adjacencies, plus a strong circulation hub for topology.",
